From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wow64win: Convert the INPUT of NtUserSendHardwareInput.

The WoW64 call passed a 32-bit process's INPUT on as it was, but
INPUT's union is 8-byte aligned in 64-bit code (MOUSEINPUT holds a
ULONG_PTR), so win32u read the hardware message from 4 bytes too
far: a HID report's WM_INPUT reached the server as message 0, and
win32u then logged "process_hardware_message unknown message type 0"
for each one, about a thousand a second for a gamepad. Only hidclass
sends these, which ran in 64-bit winedevice until a 32-bit PS5 game
started hosting it (patch 0911).

The INPUT is now converted field by field, as for NtUserSendInput.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wow64win/user.c b/dlls/wow64win/user.c
index 92c1877..9ed7ddd 100644
--- a/dlls/wow64win/user.c
+++ b/dlls/wow64win/user.c
@@ -1745,10 +1745,34 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI wow64_NtUserCallHwndParam( UINT *args )
                 ULONG input;
                 ULONG lparam;
             } *params32 = UlongToPtr( param );
+            const INPUT32 *input32 = UlongToPtr( params32->input );
             struct send_hardware_input_params params;
+            INPUT input = {.type = input32->type};
 
+            /* INPUT's union is 8-byte aligned in 64-bit code: convert it, as for NtUserSendInput. */
+            switch (input.type)
+            {
+            case INPUT_MOUSE:
+                input.mi.dx          = input32->mi.dx;
+                input.mi.dy          = input32->mi.dy;
+                input.mi.mouseData   = input32->mi.mouseData;
+                input.mi.dwFlags     = input32->mi.dwFlags;
+                input.mi.time        = input32->mi.time;
+                input.mi.dwExtraInfo = input32->mi.dwExtraInfo;
+                break;
+            case INPUT_KEYBOARD:
+                input.ki.wVk         = input32->ki.wVk;
+                input.ki.wScan       = input32->ki.wScan;
+                input.ki.dwFlags     = input32->ki.dwFlags;
+                input.ki.time        = input32->ki.time;
+                input.ki.dwExtraInfo = input32->ki.dwExtraInfo;
+                break;
+            case INPUT_HARDWARE:
+                input.hi = input32->hi;
+                break;
+            }
             params.flags = params32->flags;
-            params.input = UlongToPtr( params32->input );
+            params.input = &input;
             params.lparam = params32->lparam;
             return NtUserCallHwndParam( hwnd, (UINT_PTR)&params, code );
         }
